laurel 2150: Adreno 610 on the Mi A3 (SM6125 trinket), on by default (gpu=0 = kill switch). TopazAdreno.cpp (topaz 0901-0947) with the trinket values of the stock 4.14 kernel: zap carve-out 0x57515000, gpucc-trinket alpha PLLs (PLL0 +0x0, PLL1 +0x100, gfx3d = AUX2/2, OPPs 320-950 MHz for gpu_mhz) instead of khaje's Zonda PLL, GX GDSC without the GMU-era sw-reset/clamp registers, gcc_gpu_cfg_ahb + gcc_sys_noc_compute_sf_axi on, kgsl chip id 0x06010000 and highest bank bit 14 (NC_MODE_CNTL 0xb, UCHE_MODE_CNTL hbb). The zap shader (a610_zap.mdt + .bNN, signed for this SoC/OEM) and the SQE (a630_sqe.fw) come from the root (/usr/share/firmware/laurel, installed by scripts/laurel/root-add-gpu.sh from the phone's own vendor image); the built-in topaz SQE is the fallback, the zap has none. The 6860-byte zap metadata spans two 4 KB pages (TOPAZ_4K): the contiguous pool buffer is used. GPU pool at run time: DDR after the kernel's DarwinBoot window, [align64M(max(kernel end, 0xC0000000)), 0xE0000000) (TopazModem's pool starts at 0xE0000000), else kernel memory below 4 GiB (gpu_midmem). Self-check: one CP fence write through UCHE/SMMU/DDR after ME_INIT. One line: 'LAUREL GPU: on: Adreno 610 chip 0x06010000, core 300 MHz, zap PAS 13 at 0x57515000 (own a610_zap, ...), SQE own ..., SMMU pass-through, pool ...; RedwoodGPU published' or 'LAUREL GPU: off: <step> failed: <reason>'. A failure leaves RedwoodGPU unpublished: backboardd keeps its software renderer.

